  "content": {
    "id": "p31-q3",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Determine the dilation factor if the original graph is $y=f(x)$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p31-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=f(2x)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Horizontal by factor $\\frac12$.",
          "worked": "Replacing $x$ with $2x=\\frac{x}{(\\frac12)}$ multiplies all $x$ coordinates by $\\frac12$. Horizontal dilation by factor $\\frac12$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=f(3x)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Horizontal by factor $\\frac13$.",
          "worked": "Replacing $x$ with $3x=\\frac{x}{(\\frac13)}$ multiplies all $x$ coordinates by $\\frac13$. Horizontal dilation by factor $\\frac13$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$y=f\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Horizontal by factor $2$.",
          "worked": "Replacing $x$ with $\\frac{x}{2}$ multiplies all $x$ coordinates by $2$. Horizontal dilation by factor $2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$y=f\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Horizontal by factor $3$.",
          "worked": "Replacing $x$ with $\\frac{x}{3}$ multiplies all $x$ coordinates by $3$. Horizontal dilation by factor $3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q3-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$y=f\\left(\\frac{2x}{3}\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Horizontal by factor $\\frac32$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2x}{3}&=\\frac{x}{\\frac32}\\end{align*}$$Replacing $x$ with $\\frac{x}{(\\frac32)}$ multiplies all $x$ coordinates by $\\frac32$. Horizontal dilation by factor $\\frac32$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q3-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$y=f\\left(\\frac{3x}{2}\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Horizontal by factor $\\frac23$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3x}{2}&=\\frac{x}{\\frac23}\\end{align*}$$Replacing $x$ with $\\frac{x}{(\\frac23)}$ multiplies all $x$ coordinates by $\\frac23$. Horizontal dilation by factor $\\frac23$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q3-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$y=2f(x)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Vertical by factor $2$.",
          "worked": "All $y$ coordinates are multiplied by $2$. Vertical dilation by factor $2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q3-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$y=3f(x)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Vertical by factor $3$.",
          "worked": "All $y$ coordinates are multiplied by $3$. Vertical dilation by factor $3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q3-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$3y=f(x)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Vertical by factor $\\frac13$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3y&=f(x)\\\\y&=\\frac13f(x)\\end{align*}$$All $y$ coordinates are multiplied by $\\frac13$. Vertical dilation by factor $\\frac13$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q3-j",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$3y=2f(x)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Vertical by factor $\\frac23$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3y&=2f(x)\\\\y&=\\frac23f(x)\\end{align*}$$All $y$ coordinates are multiplied by $\\frac23$. Vertical dilation by factor $\\frac23$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q3-k",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "k",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac{f(x)}{3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Vertical by factor $\\frac13$.",
          "worked": "All $y$ coordinates are multiplied by $\\frac13$. Vertical dilation by factor $\\frac13$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q3-l",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "l",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{y}{2}=3f(x)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Vertical by factor $6$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{y}{2}&=3f(x)\\\\y&=6f(x)\\end{align*}$$All $y$ coordinates are multiplied by $6$. Vertical dilation by factor $6$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      }
    ]
